@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+---
+id: task-002-add-createdat-and-updatedat-to-tasks
+type: task
+title: "Add createdAt and updatedAt to tasks"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Record when each task was created and when it was last changed, so the app can show a task's age and
+what changed recently. Every task has `createdAt` and `updatedAt` as ISO-8601 date-time strings; the two
+are equal when a task is added, and `updatedAt` moves to the time of the change whenever a task is
+completed, reopened, renamed, tagged or untagged.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `createdAt` and `updatedAt` to the `Task` interface (`src/domain/task.ts`).
+- `createTask` now takes a third parameter, `now` (an already-formatted ISO-8601 string), and stamps
+  both fields with it.
+- `completeTask`, `reopenTask`, `renameTask`, `addTag` and `removeTag` each take a trailing `now` and set
+  `updatedAt: now` on their returned task, leaving `createdAt` untouched (it is carried over by the
+  existing `{ ...task, ... }` shallow copy).
+- `createTaskList` (`src/domain/list.ts`) now takes a mandatory `now: () => string` parameter and calls
+  it at the point of every add or change, passing the result down to the `task.ts` functions above.
+  See `dl-002` for why this had to be injected rather than read from `Date` inside the domain.
+- `createTodoList` (`src/index.ts`, outside `src/domain/`) grew an optional `now` parameter defaulting to
+  `() => new Date().toISOString()`, so the app's own entry point keeps working unchanged while tests can
+  override it.
+- Extended `test/list.test.ts` with a `fakeClock()` helper (a plain tick counter turned into an ISO
+  string, no real wall-clock or randomness, per the testing directive) and new tests covering: a new
+  task's `createdAt`/`updatedAt` on add; `updatedAt` advancing while `createdAt` stays fixed across
+  complete/reopen/rename/tag/untag; and `updatedAt` staying put when a `complete` call fails.
+- Updated the pre-existing "adds an open task" test, which asserted the full shape of a new task via
+  `deepEqual`, to include the two new fields and to use `fakeClock()` for a deterministic timestamp.
+
+All 14 tests pass (`npm test`).
